Sure! Let's break down how we can implement a recursive function to calculate the sum of elements in an array using Python. Here’s one way to do it:

```python
def recursive_list_sum(arr):
    # Base case: if the array has only one element, return that element
    if len(arr) == 1:
        return arr[0]

    # Recursive case: add the first element to the sum of the rest of the array
    return arr[0] + recursive_list_sum(arr[1:])
```

This function works by checking if the length of the array is just one element. If so, it returns that single element as the sum. Otherwise, it adds the first element (`arr[0]`) to the result of calling itself with the rest of the array (`arr[1:]`). This process continues until there is only one element left, at which point the base case is met and the recursion stops.

